  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nThursday into this weekend, upper ridging is expected to be the\ndominant force over the western U.S., extending into eastern\nMontana. This will drive above normal temperatures with at times\nhigh humidity. \n\nWeak embedded shortwaves will also keep thunderstorm chances in \nthe forecast through the weekend at times, especially in the \nevening hours.That said, the predictability of specific timing and\nplacement for convective behavior will be difficult at larger \ntime scales.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nPops were adjusted for consistency and near term collaboration.\nOtherwise, NBM largely handled the big picture trends well through\nthe forecast period. Mesoscale details will better handle\nconvective evolution in the coming days with minor additional\nadjustments expected to precipitation chances to refine timing and\nplacement mechanics. That said, confidence remains above average\nfor warm temperatures to continue through the weekend despite some\nuncertainty in specific timing of storms.",
